{"cause":"An independent R nnet::multinom comparison exposed that statsmodels MNLogit labels its first coded category as the reference, while the runtime had treated the last public category as the reference.","cause_status":"known","event_id":"4a5b6c7d-8e9f-4012-a3b4-c5d6e7f80910","event_sha256":"1fd2406aa7ff5d371db6273fae69c9f8c07a5df50c5f3d7ba4cdd47759b26d5c","evidence":{"kind":"pytest","observed_at":"2026-08-03T18:59:01.000Z","ref":"tests/test_model_families_v186.py::test_multinomial_coefficients_use_the_declared_base_category","sha256":"b02d1f5286ed0cb66dadc2dc0d771aa80675e0cbd639a478e9785b626f8528a3"},"impact":"RED: the reconstruction test observed {a: 0.34995, b: 0.33315, c: 0.31690} while the mislabeled coefficients implied {a: 0.33315, b: 0.31690, c: 0.34995}. GREEN: the runtime now codes [base_category] first, maps probabilities back to public levels, and the focused model-family suite reports 17 passed.","incident_id":"5b6c7d8e-9f01-4123-b4c5-d6e7f8091021","lesson":"Multinomial coefficients and relative-risk ratios must be labeled from the declared reference category, not from public category sort order alone.","lesson_key":"mnlogit-base-category-labels","links":["backend/workbench/engine/packs/v186_model_families/runtime.py","tests/test_model_families_v186.py"],"prev_event_sha256":"931df68a3dd87b9ddda00b5eb607d29348fa2662f610f3685cd177437d674249","preventability":"preventable","resolution":"resolved","schema_version":1,"stage":"review","subtype":"multinomial_base_category_label_mismatch","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:59:01.000Z","type":"FAILURE"}
{"cause":"The cleaned deterministic survival fixture was independently fit with R survival::coxph(Surv(duration, event) ~ x, ties = breslow) and compared field by field with the persisted Workbench packet.","cause_status":"known","event_id":"6c7d8e9f-0123-4234-a5b6-c7d8e9f01234","event_sha256":"ac5f339e7671a345faa2f161986d76b1f4ac378367140345633aa5b558aaee8c","evidence":{"kind":"r_oracle","observed_at":"2026-08-03T18:59:01.000Z","ref":"tests/test_model_families_v186.py::test_survival_cox_matches_r_survival_coxph_oracle_fixture","sha256":"b02d1f5286ed0cb66dadc2dc0d771aa80675e0cbd639a478e9785b626f8528a3"},"impact":"R_ROWS=40, R_COEF=0, R_SE=0.1414213562373095, R_P=1, R_CI=[-0.27718076486993548, 0.27718076486993548]; Python persisted COEF=0, SE=0.1414213562373095, P=1, CI=[-0.27718076486993554, 0.27718076486993554]. The declared 1e-14 CI tolerance records the cross-language qnorm/libm final-bit difference.","incident_id":"7d8e9f01-2345-4345-b6c7-d8e9f0123456","lesson":"External numerical validation must preserve the exact fixture, cleaning rule, tie method, compared fields, and declared floating-point tolerance.","lesson_key":"survival-external-oracle","links":["backend/workbench/engine/packs/v186_model_families/runtime.py","tests/test_model_families_v186.py"],"prev_event_sha256":"1fd2406aa7ff5d371db6273fae69c9f8c07a5df50c5f3d7ba4cdd47759b26d5c","preventability":"not_preventable","resolution":"resolved","schema_version":1,"stage":"review","subtype":"survival_r_oracle_verified","timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:59:01.000Z","type":"REVIEW"}
